    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4329df6c_7522ae59",
        "filename": "android/visibility.go",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 180,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-04-10T06:22:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The distinction between nil and [] doesn\u0027t seem necessary to me, and means that you can\u0027t have visibility set in a defaults module and then overridden back to [] in the real module.\n\nWhich brings up a second issue, what should the behavior of a visibility property be in a defaults module?  Set the visibility of the defaults module itself, which sometimes need to be public, or set the visibility of modules that use the defaults module?",
      "revId": "63e4e2dc3fe23e9fdd1c3d2cfe3c4dca128953a8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bf6f91d9_dc8b9d97",
        "filename": "android/visibility.go",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 180,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-04-10T14:47:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As mentioned elsewhere [] seems a little ambiguous to me. In terms of how it is implemented it would be no permissions, e.g. equivalent to //visibility:private but when defaults are used it could mean the default, which at the moment is //visibility:legacy-private but will eventually be //visibility:private. That is why visibility:[] is not valid, it must always have at least one rule.\n\nAs for the defaults you can have visibility set in a defaults module and then override that by setting visibility:[\"//visibility:private\"] or visibility:[\"//visibility:public\"].\n\nAt the moment visibility information is processed after applying the defaults and so defaults modules are not protected by visibility. I thought that defaults had to be in the same package and appear before any references so would always be visible.",
      "parentUuid": "4329df6c_7522ae59",
      "revId": "63e4e2dc3fe23e9fdd1c3d2cfe3c4dca128953a8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c5c24e4e_d8bf7cf7",
        "filename": "android/visibility.go",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 180,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-04-10T22:02:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In practice [] is unlikely to get used, I\u0027d suggest just mentioning that empty permissions means default permissions in the property docs.\n\ndefaults are just normal modules in the global namespace, so can be used from anywhere.  Is it possible to make visibility apply to them?  Could be in a followup.",
      "parentUuid": "bf6f91d9_dc8b9d97",
      "revId": "63e4e2dc3fe23e9fdd1c3d2cfe3c4dca128953a8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d3d0ef6a_ece509a3",
        "filename": "android/visibility.go",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 180,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-04-16T15:10:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That contradicts what Martin suggested in his comment above about whether visibilityRules need to be composeable. If you could come to a consensus then I will be happy to change it but don\u0027t want to change it for one reviewer only to have it rejected by another.",
      "parentUuid": "c5c24e4e_d8bf7cf7",
      "revId": "63e4e2dc3fe23e9fdd1c3d2cfe3c4dca128953a8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
